// psa.py v3.0.0 project configuration for download-speakerdeck-oracle4engineer
//
// Why PSA6003 is disabled:
//   This script and its companion intentionally use plural-noun function names
//   for functions that operate on collections of resources rather than a single
//   item. Examples in this project:
//
//     - Resolve-RuntimeDirectories  : returns a set of runtime directories
//     - Invoke-CleanupDirectories   : cleans up multiple directory trees
//     - Read-YearOverrides          : reads a table of (filename, year)
//                                     override entries
//
//   Renaming these to singular forms (e.g., -Directory) would either
//   misrepresent the function's behaviour or require breaking changes to
//   callers. The plural form is the more accurate description here, so we
//   suppress PSA6003 at the project level and document the convention in
//   SPEC.md (testing baseline).
//
//   New code added to this directory should still prefer singular nouns where
//   appropriate. PSA6003 is suppressed only because the pre-existing plural names
//   are intentional, not because the rule is unwanted in general.
{
  "disable": [
    "PSA6003"
  ]
}
